{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"deranged-declinable-xanthareel","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Prevention remediation for incident 1c0d (CI/test lane)\n\nPost-mortem: `9097-2741-6462-424c`. This is the **detection guard that would have caught the incident before prod**: a contract/regression test asserting that *any* provider transient failure degrades to a **retryable** disposition, never a hard INDETERMINATE.\n\n### Problem it guards\nA throttled primary (429/`WAIT_AND_RETRY`) that fails over to an uncredentialed fallback surfaced as `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION` → INDETERMINATE. The 1c0d fix (change 2404) added a held-out oracle for the specific keyless-`TypeError` case, but there is no *broad* contract test pinning the class invariant.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A test drives a real `build_fallback_model` chain (mocked providers, **zero live Bedrock**) where the primary raises each retryable transient (throttle 429, timeout, 5xx) and the terminal fallback arm raises a non-retryable error (credential `TypeError`, config error). Asserts the classified disposition is retryable (exit-11), never INDETERMINATE.\n- [ ] A vocabulary/closure assertion: a `FallbackExceptionGroup` is classified by its most-recoverable leg (retryable wins); an all-non-retryable group maps to `CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL`, never `NEEDS_INVESTIGATION`.\n- [ ] The test would have failed against the pre-2404 tree (confirm by reverting the two fix seams behind the sandbox).\n- [ ] Runs in the normal `make test` matrix (portable — no CI-provider-specific trigger, no network).\n\n### Notes\nThis is test-only, adds no behavior — ready to implement. Complements epic 3405-c0b7's exhaustive `exception→code` contract test (same discipline, different taxonomy: this pins the `ResolutionClass` disposition, 3405 pins the workflow error-code vocabulary).","id":"d209-4968-49be-49b0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["prevention","incident-1c0d","llm","ci","regression-oracle"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Prevention (CI/test): regression oracle — provider transient must degrade to retryable, never INDETERMINATE"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788059487228341842,"uuid":"e0f13374-8640-4928-ab8f-a023140aa1f6"}